WEBVTT

00:00:01.214 --> 00:00:02.476
Could you listen to me for a second?

00:00:02.849 --> 00:00:04.908
One day, I picked up a little fairy.

00:00:05.218 --> 00:00:09.655
But, can you believe it? The little girl can
even use magic, though she's a goofball.

00:00:10.056 --> 00:00:12.225
I'm not a goofball! I'm Sugar!

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:16.958
On top of that, weird little critters called
Salt and Pepper showed up and...

00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:21.257
Why did two more
little things have to show up?

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.970
Hey!
Don't count us like we're little critters!

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.063
My, oh-my. It is strange.

00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:27.874
- Well, Saga?
- Huh?

00:00:27.874 --> 00:00:29.273
Do you count me as a critter, too?

00:00:29.342 --> 00:00:31.537
- Sugar would be counted as a giant thing.
- What?

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:35.371
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:38.581
On my lips

00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:42.187
The rouge of tears

00:01:03.209 --> 00:01:06.212
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:06.212 --> 00:01:13.175
I don't want to know such a thing as love

00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:20.451
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:21.227 --> 00:01:23.661
On my lips

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.199
The rouge of tears

00:01:32.205 --> 00:01:35.174
On Thursdays

00:01:35.274 --> 00:01:38.175
I buy roses and...

00:01:38.244 --> 00:01:42.180
add a letter

00:01:46.219 --> 00:01:49.188
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:52.680
When I see you in my dreams

00:01:53.192 --> 00:01:57.151
you're so caring

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.209
Now, listen, Sugar. Today I don't want you
to bother me. All right?

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:14.168
I promised Norma and Anne that I'd go
shopping with them.

00:02:15.915 --> 00:02:17.075
Are you listening?

00:02:17.149 --> 00:02:21.176
I AM listening.
You're going shopping. I know.

00:02:21.454 --> 00:02:23.319
Sugar is coming with you.

00:02:23.656 --> 00:02:26.557
- No, you can't. Please don't follow me.
- What?

00:02:26.692 --> 00:02:30.389
When you're with me, my plans get
all messed up!

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:36.165
That's why we're going separate ways today!
Do NOT interrupt me. Do you understand?

00:02:36.535 --> 00:02:42.541
Huh? It's not fair! It's not fair! It's not fair!
I wanna go, too! I wanna go shopping! Shopping!

00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:44.168
Shopping! Shopping! Shopping!
See you later!

00:02:48.214 --> 00:02:49.476
Bye, I'll be back!

00:02:51.217 --> 00:02:53.082
Wait for me! Saga!

00:02:53.185 --> 00:02:54.117
Hey, Sugar!

00:02:56.188 --> 00:02:58.156
Top of the morning to you, Sugar.

00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:02.219
- Salt! Pepper!
- Well? Let's go Sugar.

00:03:02.428 --> 00:03:03.918
Huh? To where?

00:03:04.196 --> 00:03:06.164
You don't even need to ask.
To look for a "Twinkle".

00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:08.930
- What?
- Have you forgotten?

00:03:09.068 --> 00:03:13.300
Unless you find a "Twinkle",
the "Magic Flower" won't bloom.

00:03:13.372 --> 00:03:17.172
Unless the "Magic Flower" blooms, we can't
become fully-fledged Season Fairies. Right?

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.038
Ah, that's right. What shall I do?

00:03:20.212 --> 00:03:22.976
So, we'll all look for a "Twinkle".

00:03:23.215 --> 00:03:25.149
If three of us do it together,
we'll find it soon!

00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:29.176
Sure! Then, let's take off in search of
"Twinkle"! Waffo!

00:03:30.222 --> 00:03:32.156
Hey, wait a minute, Sugar!

00:03:48.207 --> 00:03:51.370
So, where is a "Twinkle"?

00:03:51.711 --> 00:03:55.169
Well, it's gotta be somewhere
in the human world.

00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:57.849
Where in the human world?

00:03:58.184 --> 00:04:01.176
What? Well, it's... um...

00:04:03.222 --> 00:04:06.658
Right here! In this scenery,
somewhere in here.

00:04:07.193 --> 00:04:09.957
What? It's so big!

00:04:10.196 --> 00:04:12.164
It'll be all right.

00:04:13.199 --> 00:04:17.470
A "Twinkle" is puffy-fluffy,
we might be able to find it very quickly.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.997
What? Doesn't a "Twinkle" twinkle?

00:04:21.207 --> 00:04:22.936
That's not true! It's comfy-warm!

00:04:23.042 --> 00:04:24.270
It's twinkle-twinkle!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.071
It's puffy-fluffy!

00:04:26.178 --> 00:04:27.543
It's comfy-warm!

00:04:27.613 --> 00:04:35.520
It's Twinkle-twinkle! Twinkle-twinkle!
It's Puffy-fluffy! Puffy-fluffy!
It's Comfy-warm! Comfy-warm!

00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:39.887
- Twinkle-twinkle! Twinkle-twinkle!
- Comfy-warm!

00:04:40.559 --> 00:04:42.993
Anyway, we'll know when we find it.

00:04:43.062 --> 00:04:44.120
That's true.

00:04:44.196 --> 00:04:46.164
But, where are we
supposed to look around?

00:04:46.499 --> 00:04:49.696
I have a pretty good idea
on the whereabouts.

00:04:56.208 --> 00:05:01.168
"Twinkles" are very important to humans
as well, I think.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.841
After all they are "Twinkles"!

00:05:04.216 --> 00:05:10.177
That's why we might find one at a place
like this where people gather.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.124
Yeah.
I have a feeling we just may find one here!

00:05:13.426 --> 00:05:14.825
Let me see...

00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:21.200
Ah! I found a "Twinkle"!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.667
- What?
- What?

00:05:25.237 --> 00:05:27.102
Is this a "Twinkle"?

00:05:27.206 --> 00:05:29.197
It's twinkling so much!

00:05:29.508 --> 00:05:31.210
But, it's not comfy-warm.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.212
It's not puffy-fluffy, either.

00:05:33.212 --> 00:05:37.148
But it's twinkling!
So, this IS the "Twinkle"!

00:05:50.229 --> 00:05:54.359
Ah! This is so cute. Look, look!

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.094
- Um, which one? This is cuter.
- Hmm... I'm not sure...

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:01.001
Ah! I'm absolutely positive!

00:06:01.107 --> 00:06:05.703
This is it! The "Twinkle"!
It is so puffy-fluffy!

00:06:06.212 --> 00:06:08.214
I found the "Twinkle"!

00:06:08.214 --> 00:06:11.741
This comfy-warm thing
must be the "Twinkle".

00:06:13.853 --> 00:06:14.820
Whoa! Hot!

00:06:18.624 --> 00:06:19.886
Twinkle-twinkle.

00:06:20.192 --> 00:06:21.159
Comfy-warm.

00:06:21.227 --> 00:06:22.421
Puffy-fluffy.

00:06:33.906 --> 00:06:38.172
What? This is..."The North Wind and the Sun"
picture book!

00:06:38.811 --> 00:06:43.874
Huh. I guess there is a story about
Season Fairies in the human world, too.

00:06:44.216 --> 00:06:47.219
Give me a break!
If I come to the human world,

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:51.123
I thought I could get away from this story!

00:06:51.123 --> 00:06:53.292
You don't like this story?

00:06:53.292 --> 00:06:58.161
It's not that, but my father tells me the story
every day.

00:06:58.497 --> 00:07:01.989
The Sun Fairy won against
the Wind Fairy, he says.

00:07:02.535 --> 00:07:05.163
I'm really tired of listening to the story!

00:07:05.871 --> 00:07:09.208
I like it no matter how many times
I listen to this story.

00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:13.212
It describes the gentleness of the
Wind Fairy very well.

00:07:13.212 --> 00:07:16.215
What? Gentleness? Where?

00:07:16.215 --> 00:07:17.978
Don't you understand?

00:07:18.217 --> 00:07:24.178
The Wind Fairy had no intention of competing
with the Sun Fairy from the beginning.

00:07:26.559 --> 00:07:33.158
The Wind Fairy knew that the traveler had
prepared a gift for his mother back home and...

00:07:33.232 --> 00:07:37.191
that he had put the gift under his coat.

00:07:39.205 --> 00:07:46.168
That's why he blew the wind hard at him so
that the traveler would not lose the present.

00:07:46.712 --> 00:07:47.679
Huh?

00:07:48.847 --> 00:07:51.748
Sugar? Salt?

00:07:54.887 --> 00:07:57.151
Hey, Saga! Could you help us?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:03.057
No. I'm shopping with Norma and Anne today.
All the plans are confirmed.

00:08:03.195 --> 00:08:08.098
Oh, well! I guess you don't mind missing
the greatest invention of the century.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:13.570
Oh, well. What a shame. What a shame.
Oh, well. What a shame.

00:08:14.073 --> 00:08:16.064
Phil! Keep up the good work!

00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:17.175
Yeah!

00:08:18.077 --> 00:08:21.513
- So, how is it?
- Not good. I can't find one!

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.172
What shall we do?

00:08:25.217 --> 00:08:30.120
Ah! A grownup Season Fairy!
Hello!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.224
Huh?

00:08:32.224 --> 00:08:33.659
- Hello.
- Hello.

00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:36.150
Are you all apprentices?

00:08:36.228 --> 00:08:39.254
I'm a Snow Fairy apprentice, Sugar.

00:08:39.565 --> 00:08:41.965
I'm a Sun Fairy apprentice, Salt.

00:08:42.201 --> 00:08:45.170
I'm a Wind Fairy apprentice, Pepper.

00:08:45.571 --> 00:08:48.574
- Excuse me... um...
- Well... um...

00:08:48.574 --> 00:08:53.145
Ginger. I'm a Rain Fairy Ginger.
Well, I'm still on duty. So...

00:08:53.145 --> 00:08:55.447
- Whoa! Please wait! - Whoa! Please wait!
- Whoa! Please wait!

00:08:55.447 --> 00:08:56.215
What is it?

00:08:56.215 --> 00:08:59.013
Do you know where "Twinkles" are?

00:08:59.218 --> 00:09:03.222
To find one on your own is part of your study.
Right?

00:09:03.222 --> 00:09:05.349
Well, keep at it!

00:09:07.126 --> 00:09:10.721
- How attractive.
- Really. I wish I could be like her.

00:09:10.963 --> 00:09:15.798
Yes! Yes! Sugar wants to be a fully-fledged
Snow Fairy very soon!

00:09:15.934 --> 00:09:18.203
Me, too! But, to do that...

00:09:18.203 --> 00:09:20.171
Let's find a "Twinkle" quickly!

00:09:20.906 --> 00:09:21.634
- Yup!
- Yup!

00:09:37.189 --> 00:09:39.157
It's puffy-fluffy.

00:09:40.092 --> 00:09:44.188
It's comfy-warm! Ah! Could it be... this is...

00:09:44.396 --> 00:09:45.597
- the "Twinkle"?
- The "Twinkle"?

00:09:45.597 --> 00:09:48.691
No, it's not. These are waffo!

00:09:49.001 --> 00:09:49.831
- Waffo?
- Waffo?

00:09:50.469 --> 00:09:53.802
- Give us some waffles, please.
- Yes. Welcome!

00:09:54.306 --> 00:09:55.796
Well, what are you gonna have?

00:09:56.041 --> 00:09:58.805
Let's see. What shall I have?
Ugh!

00:10:00.212 --> 00:10:01.543
Ah, Saga!

00:10:02.014 --> 00:10:05.347
What's wrong, Saga?
Uh, nothing... nothing at all!

00:10:06.518 --> 00:10:08.179
Two plains, please.

00:10:26.205 --> 00:10:29.003
Ah, It's so good!

00:10:29.208 --> 00:10:32.075
Uh, Saga! You've already finished one?

00:10:32.211 --> 00:10:37.012
What? Uh, yes. I guess I was hungry.

00:10:38.617 --> 00:10:41.220
Ah-hah!
The item I bought earlier...

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:45.224
See? Look at this. Isn't this cute?

00:10:45.224 --> 00:10:46.486
See? See? See?

00:10:46.592 --> 00:10:51.928
This is a new style by a famous designer.
Don't you think it's cute?

00:10:52.197 --> 00:10:53.198
Uh? Sure...

00:10:53.198 --> 00:10:55.901
Saga, aren't you shopping for anything today?

00:10:55.901 --> 00:10:58.927
What? For me browsing is enough.

00:10:59.204 --> 00:11:01.297
Then Anne? What about you?

00:11:01.373 --> 00:11:06.003
Me? To tell you the truth, there's a skirt
I'm not sure about buying or not.

00:11:06.211 --> 00:11:10.079
If that's the case, we'll help you decide
if it looks good on you or not.

00:11:10.449 --> 00:11:11.416
Good. Thank you.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.219
Count on us! Ah-ha!

00:11:14.219 --> 00:11:17.188
The new skirts by this designer
have just been released!

00:11:17.656 --> 00:11:20.192
- They may look good on you, Anne.
- Uh. Wel...

00:11:20.192 --> 00:11:22.786
Just a minute, Norma.
I'm not really... um...

00:11:22.861 --> 00:11:26.627
Don't be shy. It'll be fine.
Leave it to Norma!

00:11:26.932 --> 00:11:29.162
Um, Saga, I want to eat more.

00:11:29.435 --> 00:11:33.565
- This is it! Be happy with what you got.
- It wasn't enough!

00:11:33.672 --> 00:11:35.606
Don't whine like that! Hmm...

00:11:51.523 --> 00:11:52.182
Waffo!

00:11:52.925 --> 00:11:54.984
Wow! All-we-can-eat!

00:11:57.262 --> 00:11:59.025
Ah! It's like a dream!

00:12:03.202 --> 00:12:05.170
Saga, shall we get going?

00:12:05.871 --> 00:12:07.805
Yup. Let's go!

00:12:19.751 --> 00:12:20.718
A "Twinkle"?

00:12:21.286 --> 00:12:22.253
- What?
- What?

00:12:23.655 --> 00:12:26.215
- Did you say a "Twinkle"?
- Which way is it?

00:12:26.458 --> 00:12:27.823
Over there.

00:12:39.838 --> 00:12:40.998
It's a "Twinkle"!

00:12:41.306 --> 00:12:44.332
- We did it!
- Let me see it, too.

00:12:44.977 --> 00:12:47.241
Sure. I'll be right there!

00:12:50.115 --> 00:12:51.082
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:51.216 --> 00:12:53.150
Hmm... Huh?

00:12:53.218 --> 00:12:54.185
What's wrong?

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.042
What's up with him?

00:13:17.042 --> 00:13:19.943
I don't know why, but he is very upset.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.739
Oh, no! What are you doing?
Don't come this way!

00:13:32.758 --> 00:13:33.759
Sugar!

00:13:33.759 --> 00:13:36.523
Good. Now is the time!

00:13:53.211 --> 00:13:55.179
Oh, dear. Huh?

00:13:57.883 --> 00:13:59.111
Uh, please wait.

00:14:01.486 --> 00:14:02.544
How is it?

00:14:03.221 --> 00:14:05.357
Hmm, not exactly.

00:14:05.357 --> 00:14:06.792
You think so?

00:14:06.792 --> 00:14:10.819
Hold on a minute. Well...
Let's see... Ah!

00:14:11.196 --> 00:14:13.765
This one is better!

00:14:13.765 --> 00:14:15.960
Uh... that is a little...

00:14:17.202 --> 00:14:20.706
I see. You're right. It's a little conservative.

00:14:20.706 --> 00:14:22.936
I'm gonna find you a more wild one!

00:14:23.208 --> 00:14:27.736
What? Uh, Norma, what do you think of
this one?

00:14:28.213 --> 00:14:31.182
- The design is not exactly sharp.
- Then, what about this?

00:14:31.249 --> 00:14:35.220
Anne, are you selecting with a plan
and a budget?

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.949
What if I choose one for you?

00:14:37.222 --> 00:14:38.849
See? How about this one?

00:14:42.494 --> 00:14:43.461
Please wait.

00:14:44.196 --> 00:14:45.356
This one is definitely better!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:02.847
Huh?

00:15:03.782 --> 00:15:07.052
It broke. The "Rain Genie EX-2".

00:15:07.052 --> 00:15:08.952
We put so much effort into it.

00:15:09.021 --> 00:15:11.223
A failure is a shortcut to success!

00:15:11.223 --> 00:15:13.825
It means the next one will be a big success.

00:15:13.825 --> 00:15:16.521
All right!
To create rainfall anytime, anywhere.

00:15:16.728 --> 00:15:20.164
We'll work hard for the creation of
the "Rain Genie EX-3"!

00:15:20.399 --> 00:15:21.297
- Hurray! - Hurray!
- Hurray!

00:15:21.466 --> 00:15:24.264
- Hurray! Hurray! - Hurray! Hurray!
- Hurray! Hurray!

00:15:28.373 --> 00:15:30.807
- Good.
- He's not gonna find us here.

00:15:37.816 --> 00:15:39.181
Whoa! Why?

00:15:39.418 --> 00:15:41.181
Whoa! Run! Whoa!

00:15:42.187 --> 00:15:44.178
No! No! No! No! No! No!

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.179
Huh?

00:15:47.225 --> 00:15:49.955
Why is he only after me?

00:15:50.796 --> 00:15:51.763
Sugar!

00:15:56.234 --> 00:15:57.201
Where am I?

00:15:58.236 --> 00:16:00.363
No! No! No! No! No! No! No!

00:16:04.643 --> 00:16:05.735
NO!

00:16:17.189 --> 00:16:19.680
Are you all right, Sugar?

00:16:23.762 --> 00:16:27.289
You're fine.
Mr. Crow is passed out.

00:16:27.632 --> 00:16:30.202
Quick! Let me out! Please!

00:16:30.202 --> 00:16:31.203
The problem is...

00:16:31.203 --> 00:16:32.771
the door is stuck shut.

00:16:32.771 --> 00:16:34.739
What? You must be kidding!

00:16:42.214 --> 00:16:43.977
We'll get you out very soon.

00:16:44.216 --> 00:16:46.616
Until then, please keep quiet.

00:16:47.319 --> 00:16:48.149
Yes.

00:16:48.253 --> 00:16:51.450
- But how?
- Let me think...

00:16:53.225 --> 00:16:55.227
Hey, Phil. What about this one?

00:16:55.227 --> 00:16:57.422
Well, just put it in!

00:16:57.662 --> 00:16:59.152
Phil, how about this?

00:16:59.231 --> 00:17:03.565
I want something longer.
Could you look for something else?

00:17:04.202 --> 00:17:06.796
Let's ask them to help us out.

00:17:07.038 --> 00:17:08.164
No other choice, I guess.

00:17:09.207 --> 00:17:11.643
Let's see. Can I use this?

00:17:11.643 --> 00:17:15.213
Hey! Come over here and rescue Sugar!
O. K?

00:17:15.213 --> 00:17:18.705
I beg of you.
Please rescue Sugar immediately!

00:17:18.984 --> 00:17:20.144
I don't think so.

00:17:20.485 --> 00:17:21.452
- What?
- What?

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.545
Are there anything bigger?

00:17:23.822 --> 00:17:26.382
Ah!
I might be able to use this!

00:17:26.491 --> 00:17:28.425
He doesn't notice us.

00:17:29.261 --> 00:17:31.491
- If that's the case, I'll use "that".
- That?

00:17:34.199 --> 00:17:36.167
With this, take them to where Sugar is...

00:17:44.676 --> 00:17:46.011
This is it! This!

00:17:46.011 --> 00:17:48.411
Salt, please keep doing a good job!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.856
Ah! He seems to have noticed.

00:17:57.856 --> 00:18:00.017
Somehow it's getting warm.

00:18:00.892 --> 00:18:02.723
Hey, Phil, come here for a second!

00:18:02.894 --> 00:18:03.758
What is it?

00:18:03.929 --> 00:18:06.591
Ah! He's gone.

00:18:07.465 --> 00:18:09.057
I can't do it any more!

00:18:09.267 --> 00:18:09.699
Salt!

00:18:12.337 --> 00:18:15.170
Let me have a chance this time!

00:18:17.709 --> 00:18:19.711
Gently, gently, softly, softly...

00:18:19.711 --> 00:18:24.171
Wind, Wind, take everyone to
where Sugar is.

00:18:27.519 --> 00:18:28.986
Ah, this is cool!

00:18:29.221 --> 00:18:30.188
Isn't it? Isn't it?

00:18:30.288 --> 00:18:32.415
There are more over there.

00:18:32.557 --> 00:18:35.492
Really? Good. Let's go collect them.

00:18:36.194 --> 00:18:39.391
Uh! Not over there. This way, please.

00:18:40.198 --> 00:18:41.165
Please notice!

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.189
Oh, no! Oh, no!

00:18:44.236 --> 00:18:47.171
Oh, no! Oh, no!

00:18:48.206 --> 00:18:50.174
It's kind of a weird wind.

00:19:02.454 --> 00:19:06.413
Please get me out soon, Salt and Pepper.

00:19:17.269 --> 00:19:20.432
- Why don't they notice us?
- We have a problem.

00:19:21.306 --> 00:19:24.332
- Are you all right, Sugar?
- Yes...

00:19:24.476 --> 00:19:27.679
- Please cheer up.
- Yes...

00:19:27.679 --> 00:19:31.137
If that person were here, it would be
a piece of cake.

00:19:31.216 --> 00:19:34.219
Please be patient a little longer, Sugar.

00:19:34.219 --> 00:19:36.619
We'll try one more time.

00:19:36.821 --> 00:19:39.756
Those guys.
How can I make them notice us?

00:19:39.891 --> 00:19:41.586
I wish there was a good trick.

00:19:42.227 --> 00:19:45.924
Saga would notice us right away.

00:19:46.197 --> 00:19:49.166
You're right. Miss Saga would...

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:54.761
Hey! Have you come to help me?

00:19:55.206 --> 00:19:58.232
Uh... no. It's not that.
Just looking for something.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.177
See you later!

00:20:00.412 --> 00:20:01.845
Uh! Wait a minute!

00:20:06.217 --> 00:20:10.051
Come on. It was a bad idea to play
in a dangerous place!

00:20:10.322 --> 00:20:12.256
It's exasperating!

00:20:14.192 --> 00:20:15.293
Saga!

00:20:15.293 --> 00:20:17.853
Thank you, Saga, for rescuing me!

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:19.858
O.K. O.K.

00:20:20.332 --> 00:20:21.594
Thank you Pepper.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.958
Thank you, Salt.

00:20:24.736 --> 00:20:28.103
Hey, stop it! Don't!
After all, this is how it turns out, I guess.

00:20:28.206 --> 00:20:29.195
Hey, Saga!

00:20:30.408 --> 00:20:32.376
Have you found what you were looking for?

00:20:38.283 --> 00:20:40.046
Huh, just a broken bell?

00:20:40.251 --> 00:20:41.912
- What? - What?
- What?

00:20:41.987 --> 00:20:45.184
- A bell? Isn't that a "Twinkle"?
- No, it's not.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.823
Don't tell me that...

00:20:49.227 --> 00:20:51.286
Hey, Joe! It's you again!

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:52.697
You said Joe?

00:20:53.198 --> 00:20:54.563
It's the name of that crow.

00:20:54.733 --> 00:20:58.169
When he sees something that twinkles,
he snatches it away instantly.

00:20:59.204 --> 00:21:02.696
I see... something that twinkles...

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:16.414
I'm exhausted.

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:23.559
Hmm. It feels good.
Now I've started feeling comfy-warm.

00:21:23.762 --> 00:21:27.562
Really. It's puffy-fluffy and very pleasant.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.804
It's twinkling!

00:21:35.173 --> 00:21:38.108
- Twinkle-twinkle! - Comfy-warm!
- Puffy-fluffy!

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:40.007
"Twinkles"!

00:21:43.314 --> 00:21:44.838
This is it!

00:21:47.185 --> 00:21:50.120
Hey! Have all of you finished
shampooing?

00:21:52.857 --> 00:21:54.916
- I don't like shampoo!
- Run!

00:21:57.095 --> 00:22:00.861
- No, no, no! I don't want to.
- I don't want to!
Here is a shower attack!

00:22:01.232 --> 00:22:08.195
- Oh, no. Don't! I don't like it!
- I don't want to. No, no, no!
No matter what, I'll wash it today!
Wearing a cap all day makes hair dirty!

00:22:20.919 --> 00:22:24.411
Wishes upon the Moon

00:22:25.523 --> 00:22:28.515
Melting in the water

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:33.859
I found a street lined with trees

00:22:34.566 --> 00:22:38.195
Songs of stardust

00:22:39.804 --> 00:22:47.074
The breeze crossing over
the Bridge of Rainbows

00:22:47.512 --> 00:22:53.084
You already knew...

00:22:53.084 --> 00:22:56.952
the happiness of connecting our hearts

00:22:57.655 --> 00:22:58.917
Sugar Snow

00:23:00.058 --> 00:23:06.759
When powdery snow whirls in town

00:23:07.999 --> 00:23:11.526
the season of flower blossoms is near...

00:23:13.171 --> 00:23:16.038
and, I think of you.

00:23:18.676 --> 00:23:24.876
The love that melts our hearts and...

00:23:25.517 --> 00:23:35.984
the dreams are in your heart

00:23:39.964 --> 00:23:43.024
Preview of the Next Episode
Well, out of the blue, I'll give you a quiz!

00:23:43.201 --> 00:23:44.202
A quiz?

00:23:44.202 --> 00:23:45.203
Here's a question.

00:23:45.203 --> 00:23:49.307
What's something "twinkle-twinkle",
"comfy-warm" and "puffy-fluffy"?

00:23:49.307 --> 00:23:53.243
If you have the answer, let Sugar know quietly.
Everyone, I'm looking forward to it!

00:23:53.311 --> 00:23:57.907
By any chance, aren't you trying to cut
corners in finding a "Twinkle"?

00:23:58.082 --> 00:24:00.846
Uh... Saga is pretty quick.

00:24:01.219 --> 00:24:04.780
"A Little Snow Fairy, Sugar"
The next episode is
"Where are the"Twinkles"?"

00:24:05.190 --> 00:24:07.750
What? A "Twinkle" in such a place?
